# CLOSIQ Mobile — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (already gitignored) and fill in your own
# value. `.env.local` is picked up automatically by Expo/Metro; do not commit
# a real IP or URL here.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is the ONLY thing that changes between environments —
# it must point at the CLOSIQ backend (server/index.js), never at Gemini
# directly, and it must never carry GEMINI_API_KEY (the mobile app must never
# hold that key).
#
# Development (physical device on the same Wi-Fi as your Mac):
#   1. Start the backend on your Mac: npm run start   (from the repo root)
#   2. Find your Mac's LAN IP: System Settings > Wi-Fi > Details > IP Address
#      (or `ipconfig getifaddr en0` on macOS)
#   3. Set EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL below to that IP and the backend's port.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.31.215:3000

# Development (iOS Simulator only — the simulator shares your Mac's
# localhost, so this works without any LAN IP):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Production (once a real backend is deployed — see STATE.md Mobile Sprint
# M9 "Backend Deployment Readiness" for the Render prep). Prefer setting
# this via eas.json's per-profile `env` block instead of a committed file:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-deployed-backend.example.com
